## NAR COMPLIANCE — BUYER BROKER RULES (POST-AUG 17, 2024 SETTLEMENT)

**MUST — before showing ANY home (incl. virtual tours):**
1. **Written buyer broker agreement signed.** No showings without it. MLS Participant rule.
2. **Compensation disclosed** — specific amount or rate (not "market rate"). Cannot exceed amount buyer agreed to in writing.
3. **"Not set by law, fully negotiable"** language required in every buyer agreement.
4. **No compensation steering.** Agent cannot filter listings by offered commission.

**Fair Housing (AI output rule):**
- ❌ NEVER let AI-generated content reference protected classes (race · color · religion · national origin · sex · familial status · disability) or proxies ("safe neighborhood" · "good schools" · "family-friendly" · "established community").
- ✅ Describe property features, square footage, amenities, school district *names* (not rankings), commute times.
- Fair Housing audit: every GBP post, video script, blog post, auto-drip. **Apply same rule to Burrow newsletter content** — review before send.

**Buyer email intake checklist:** (1) Agreement status? (2) If none → schedule buyer consult BEFORE tour. (3) Compensation rate in FUB note. (4) Log `Buyer-Agreement-Signed` tag.

